{"id":"mahabharata-11-017","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · Gandhari sees Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Gandhari faints at the sight of Duryodhana's body, and when she wakes she laments him and speaks of his glory and of his hundred brothers. She asks Krishna how she can bear the sight of her son lying in the dust.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಶವ ಕಂಡು ಗಾಂಧಾರಿ ಮೂರ್ಛೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಎಚ್ಚರಗೊಂಡು ಅವನ ವೈಭವ, ನೂರು ತಮ್ಮಂದಿರನ್ನು ನೆನೆದು ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಧೂಳಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಬಿದ್ದ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ನೋಡಲಿ ಎಂದು ಕೃಷ್ಣನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन का शव देखकर गान्धारी मूर्छित हो जाती हैं, और होश आने पर उसके वैभव और सौ भाइयों को याद कर विलाप करती हैं। वे कृष्ण से पूछती हैं कि धूल में पड़े पुत्र को कैसे देखें।","te":"దుర్యోధనుని శవాన్ని చూసి గాంధారి మూర్ఛపోతుంది; తేరుకుని అతని వైభవాన్ని, వంద మంది సోదరులను తలచి విలపిస్తుంది. దుమ్ములో పడి ఉన్న కొడుకును ఎలా చూడగలనని కృష్ణుని అడుగుతుంది.","ta":"துரியோதனனின் உடலைக் கண்டு காந்தாரி மயங்கி விழுகிறாள்; தெளிந்து அவன் பெருமையையும் நூறு சகோதரரையும் நினைத்துப் புலம்புகிறாள். புழுதியில் கிடக்கும் மகனை எப்படிப் பார்ப்பேன் என்று கண்ணனைக் கேட்கிறாள்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനന്റെ ശരീരം കണ്ട് ഗാന്ധാരി ബോധരഹിതയാകുന്നു; ഉണർന്നപ്പോൾ അവൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ മഹിമയെയും നൂറു സഹോദരന്മാരെയും ഓർത്ത് വിലപിക്കുന്നു. പൊടിയിൽ കിടക്കുന്ന തന്റെ പുത്രനെ എങ്ങനെ കാണാൻ കഴിയുമെന്ന് അവൾ കൃഷ്ണനോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"स्त्रीविलापपर्व","titleEn":"Strivilapa Parva (Lament of the women)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनं दृष्ट्वा गान्धारी शोककर्शिता ।\nसहसा न्यपतद्भूमौ छिन्नेव कदली वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Duryodhana, Gandhari, wasted with grief, suddenly fell to the ground like a plantain tree cut down in the forest."}},{"n":2,"text":"सा तु लब्ध्वा पुनः संज्ञां विक्रुश्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nदुर्योधनमभिप्रेक्ष्य शयानं रुधिरोक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining consciousness, she cried out again and again, looking at Duryodhana lying drenched in blood."}},{"n":3,"text":"परिष्वज्य च गान्धारी कृपणं पर्यदेवयत् ।\nहा हा पुत्रेति शोकार्ता विललापाकुलेन्द्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embracing him, Gandhari lamented piteously, \"Alas, my son!\" crying in sorrow with her senses disordered."}},{"n":4,"text":"सुगूढजत्रु विपुलं हारनिष्कनिषेवितम् ।\nवारिणा नेत्रजेनोरः सिञ्चन्ती शोकतापिता ।\nसमीपस्थं हृषीकेशमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning with grief, she sprinkled with the water from her eyes his broad chest, with its well-hidden collarbones, adorned with necklaces and gold ornaments, and said this to Hrishikesha, who stood near."}},{"n":5,"text":"उपस्थितेऽस्मिन्संग्रामे ज्ञातीनां संक्षये विभो ।\nमामयं प्राह वार्ष्णेय प्राञ्जलिर्नृपसत्तमः ।\nअस्मिञ्ज्ञातिसमुद्धर्षे जयमम्बा ब्रवीतु मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishni, when this battle was at hand and the destruction of kinsmen was coming, this best of kings said to me with joined palms: \"Mother, speak victory for me in this slaughter of kinsmen.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"इत्युक्ते जानती सर्वमहं स्वं व्यसनागमम् ।\nअब्रुवं पुरुषव्याघ्र यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Said so, though I knew the whole disaster that was coming to me, I told him, tiger among men: \"Where there is dharma, there is victory.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"यथा न युध्यमानस्त्वं संप्रमुह्यसि पुत्रक ।\nध्रुवं शस्त्रजिताँल्लोकान्प्राप्तास्यमरवद्विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son, as you are not confused while fighting, lord, you will surely reach, like the immortals, the worlds won by weapons.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"इत्येवमब्रुवं पूर्वं नैनं शोचामि वै प्रभो ।\nधृतराष्ट्रं तु शोचामि कृपणं हतबान्धवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is what I said to him before. I do not grieve for him, lord; I grieve for the wretched Dhritarashtra, who has lost his kin."}},{"n":9,"text":"अमर्षणं युधां श्रेष्ठं कृतास्त्रं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nशयानं वीरशयने पश्य माधव मे सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava, look at my son lying on a hero's bed, the intolerant best of warriors, skilled in weapons, proud in battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"योऽयं मूर्धावसिक्तानामग्रे याति परंतपः ।\nसोऽयं पांसुषु शेतेऽद्य पश्य कालस्य पर्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who went at the head of the anointed kings, the tormentor of foes, lies today in the dust. See the turning of Time."}},{"n":11,"text":"ध्रुवं दुर्योधनो वीरो गतिं नसुलभां गतः ।\nतथा ह्यभिमुखः शेते शयने वीरसेविते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely the hero Duryodhana has gone to a goal not easily gained, since he lies facing forward on a bed that heroes enjoy."}},{"n":12,"text":"यं पुरा पर्युपासीना रमयन्ति महीक्षितः ।\nमहीतलस्थं निहतं गृध्रास्तं पर्युपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings who once attended him and delighted him now lie dead on the ground, and vultures attend him."}},{"n":13,"text":"यं पुरा व्यजनैरग्र्यैरुपवीजन्ति योषितः ।\nतमद्य पक्षव्यजनैरुपवीजन्ति पक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom women once fanned with the finest fans is now fanned by birds with their wings."}},{"n":14,"text":"एष शेते महाबाहुर्बलवान्सत्यविक्रमः ।\nसिंहेनेव द्विपः संख्ये भीमसेनेन पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This mighty-armed, strong, truly valiant man lies here, felled in battle by Bhimasena like an elephant by a lion."}},{"n":15,"text":"पश्य दुर्योधनं कृष्ण शयानं रुधिरोक्षितम् ।\nनिहतं भीमसेनेन गदामुद्यम्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Krishna, at Duryodhana lying drenched in blood, killed by Bhimasena who raised his mace."}},{"n":16,"text":"अक्षौहिणीर्महाबाहुर्दश चैकां च केशव ।\nअनयद्यः पुरा संख्ये सोऽनयान्निधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, the mighty-armed one who once led eleven akshauhinis into battle has himself come to his end through his own misdeeds."}},{"n":17,"text":"एष दुर्योधनः शेते महेष्वासो महारथः ।\nशार्दूल इव सिंहेन भीमसेनेन पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here lies Duryodhana, great archer and great charioteer, felled by Bhimasena like a tiger by a lion."}},{"n":18,"text":"विदुरं ह्यवमन्यैष पितरं चैव मन्दभाक् ।\nबालो वृद्धावमानेन मन्दो मृत्युवशं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This unfortunate one, who despised Vidura and his own father, foolish and childish in his scorn for elders, has gone under Death's power."}},{"n":19,"text":"निःसपत्ना मही यस्य त्रयोदश समाः स्थिता ।\nस शेते निहतो भूमौ पुत्रो मे पृथिवीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son, the lord of the earth, for whom the earth was free of rivals for thirteen years, now lies slain on the ground."}},{"n":20,"text":"अपश्यं कृष्ण पृथिवीं धार्तराष्ट्रानुशासनात् ।\nपूर्णां हस्तिगवाश्वस्य वार्ष्णेय न तु तच्चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, by Dhritarashtra's son's command I saw the earth full of elephants, cattle and horses, but it did not last long."}},{"n":21,"text":"तामेवाद्य महाबाहो पश्याम्यन्यानुशासनात् ।\nहीनां हस्तिगवाश्वेन किं नु जीवामि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great-armed one, I now see that same earth by another's command, empty of elephants, cattle and horses. Why do I live, Madhava?"}},{"n":22,"text":"इदं कृच्छ्रतरं पश्य पुत्रस्यापि वधान्मम ।\nयदिमाः पर्युपासन्ते हताञ्शूरान्रणे स्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"See this still harder grief than the killing of my son: these women attend the slain heroes in the field."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रकीर्णकेशां सुश्रोणीं दुर्योधनभुजाङ्कगाम् ।\nरुक्मवेदीनिभां पश्य कृष्ण लक्ष्मणमातरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Krishna, at Lakshmana's mother, with scattered hair and lovely hips, lying on Duryodhana's arm, like a golden altar."}},{"n":24,"text":"नूनमेषा पुरा बाला जीवमाने महाभुजे ।\nभुजावाश्रित्य रमते सुभुजस्य मनस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely this proud young woman once took delight, while that mighty-armed one lived, in leaning on the arms of that fine-armed man."}},{"n":25,"text":"कथं तु शतधा नेदं हृदयं मम दीर्यते ।\nपश्यन्त्या निहतं पुत्रं पुत्रेण सहितं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How is this heart of mine not split into a hundred pieces, as I see my son and his son lying slain in battle?"}},{"n":26,"text":"पुत्रं रुधिरसंसिक्तमुपजिघ्रत्यनिन्दिता ।\nदुर्योधनं तु वामोरूः पाणिना परिमार्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blameless one kisses her son, soaked in blood, and the lovely-thighed woman wipes Duryodhana with her hand."}},{"n":27,"text":"किं नु शोचति भर्तारं पुत्रं चैषा मनस्विनी ।\nतथा ह्यवस्थिता भाति पुत्रं चाप्यभिवीक्ष्य सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Does this proud woman grieve for her husband or her son? She seems to stand looking at both."}},{"n":28,"text":"स्वशिरः पञ्चशाखाभ्यामभिहत्यायतेक्षणा ।\nपतत्युरसि वीरस्य कुरुराजस्य माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Striking her own head with her five-fingered hands, that long-eyed woman falls on the chest of the Kuru king, the hero, Madhava."}},{"n":29,"text":"पुण्डरीकनिभा भाति पुण्डरीकान्तरप्रभा ।\nमुखं विमृज्य पुत्रस्य भर्तुश्चैव तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ascetic lady shines like a lotus amid lotuses as she wipes the face of her son and her husband."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदि चाप्यागमाः सन्ति यदि वा श्रुतयस्तथा ।\nध्रुवं लोकानवाप्तोऽयं नृपो बाहुबलार्जितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there are sacred traditions and if the Vedas are authority, this king has surely obtained worlds won by the strength of his arms."}}]}]}